WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:04.334
You'd persuade rather than force.

2
00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:09.216
And you keep that standard when the force would come through a vote, a law,

3
00:00:09.216 --> 00:00:09.986
or a leader.

4
00:00:14.386 --> 00:00:18.367
On the map, you landed somewhere up here, near the line.

5
00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:20.113
One standard, both ways.

6
00:00:20.113 --> 00:00:25.699
Most people draw the line at their own hands, and hand the rest to someone else.

7
00:00:26.599 --> 00:00:32.095
The Principle of Human Respect says your standard is right, and says why.

8
00:00:32.095 --> 00:00:38.036
Coercion, theft, and violence always reduce happiness, harmony, and prosperity.

9
00:00:38.036 --> 00:00:38.630
Always.

10
00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:42.344
Whose hand is on them doesn't change what they do.

11
00:00:43.244 --> 00:00:45.364
The harder test comes next.

12
00:00:45.364 --> 00:00:48.015
Find the cause you care about most.

13
00:00:53.415 --> 00:00:58.117
And ask whether any part of it still depends on making people go along.
